---
layout: base.njk
permalink: "/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ site.name }} — truck alternatives and labor-only help when U-Haul is sold out"
  description: "{{ site.description }}"
  breadcrumbs:
    - name: Home
      url: /
---
<section class="page-hero wrap">
  {% include "partials/breadcrumbs.njk" %}
  <p class="eyebrow">A public-source directory</p>
  <h1>{{ site.tagline }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ site.description }} We only list hours, truck types, and services that a business publishes, and we date every check. If we cannot verify it, it does not go on the page. We do not cache live truck inventory — reserve on the company’s own site.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap" id="cities">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Cities</h2>
    <p class="muted">Each city is one data file, so a new page can ship as soon as the listings are verified.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="city-grid">
    {% for city in cities %}
    <li>
      <a class="city-card" href="{{ city | cityPath }}">
        <h3>{{ city.city }}, {{ city.state }}</h3>
        <p>{% if city.focus %}{{ city.focus }} focus · {% endif %}{{ city.listings | length }} listings</p>
        <p class="small muted">Updated {{ city.lastUpdated | displayDate }}</p>
      </a>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap tonight">
  <h2>Why this directory exists</h2>
  <p>People looking for a truck often find that a U-Haul reservation was cancelled, or that no trucks are left on pickup day. This site is for the other options: other rental counters that still publish locations and hours, and labor-only crews who will load a truck or container you already have.</p>
  <p><a href="/guides/uhaul-sold-out-every-other-way-to-move-this-weekend/">Read the sold-out weekend guide</a> · <a href="/about/">How we research listings</a></p>
</section>
